# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE ignore list
#
# Every entry MUST include:
#   - CVE identifier
#   - Reason for ignoring (e.g. "not exploitable in this context because...")
#   - Owner (GitHub username)
#   - Expiry date (YYYY-MM-DD) — re-evaluate when this date passes
#
# Example:
# CVE-XXXX-XXXXX # reason: not exploitable in this context | owner: @mirusser | expires: 2026-12-01

# CVE-2026-4878 # reason: libcap2 TOCTOU in cap_set_file() requires local write access to a parent directory — not reachable in a containerized non-root workload (APP_UID 1654, no cap_set_file usage in application code); suppress until aspnet:10.0 base image includes libcap2 1:2.66-5ubuntu2.4 | owner: @mirusser | expires: 2026-12-01

# kubernetes-mcp-server v0.0.66 (vendored, checksum-pinned per scripts/kubernetes-mcp-server.manifest.json —
# see deploy/docker/mcp-gateway.Dockerfile for why we pin an official upstream release rather than build
# from source). Each CVE below is already fixed in the underlying Go module/toolchain, but v0.0.66 was
# built against the older, vulnerable versions and no newer kubernetes-mcp-server release exists yet
# (checked https://github.com/containers/kubernetes-mcp-server/releases on 2026-08-23; v0.0.66 is latest).
# Re-evaluate at expiry: bump scripts/kubernetes-mcp-server.manifest.json if a newer release is out,
# otherwise renew after re-checking upstream release notes.
